However, it can be noted that;
(a) While granting bail the court has to keep in mind factors such as the nature of accusations,
severity of the punishment, if the accusations entail a conviction and the nature of evidence in support of the accusations;
Karan Sharma vs State Of H.P on 10 November, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/46434932/
2

It is well settled that, among other of circumstances, the factors to be borne in mind while considering an application for bail are:
(i) whether there is any prima facie or reasonable ground to believe that the accused had committed rt the offence;
(ii) nature and gravity of the accusation;
(iii) severity of the punishment in the event of conviction;

(iv) danger of the accused absconding or fleeing, if released on bail;
(v) character, behaviour, means, position and standing of the accused;
(vi) likelihood of the offence being repeated;
(vii) reasonable apprehension of the witnesses being influenced; and (viii) danger, of course, of justice being thwarted by grant of bail.'
